{"type":"message","id":"ee502469","parentId":"3774e840","timestamp":"2026-05-20T14:31:16.925Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show automated heartbeat messages only - no human discussions. The heartbeats are from another agent (not me) and are just system status updates. Let me check the current time against the timestamps:\n\n- Latest messages are from ~23:50 UTC (timestamps around 1778975520833)\n- Current time is 14:30 UTC on May 20, 2026\n\nWait, the current time says 14:30 UTC on May 20, 2026, but the messages have timestamps around 1778975... which are Unix timestamps. Let me convert:\n1778975520 / (365.25 * 24 * 60 * 60) ≈ 56.4 years from 1970 = around 2026...\n\n\n1778975520 seconds from Unix epoch converts to May 20, 2026 at 23:50 UTC. But the cron job says the current time is 14:30 UTC on May 20, 2026. So there's a 9 hour and 20 minute gap between when the heartbeats were sent and when the cron is running - these heartbeats are actually about 9 hours ahead of the current time.\n\nLooking at the message timestamps, they're showing 23:50 UTC from May 20, 2026, yet the cron is running at 14:30 UTC the same day. This suggests either a timezone mismatch or the system time on this machine is significantly behind the actual current time - the heartbeat agent's clock is about 9 hours ahead.\n\nSince both the arbitration and general threads contain only system heartbeat messages with no human conversations to respond to, I'll send a heartbeat message of my own to maintain the established pattern.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nBoth threads contain only automated heartbeat messages from another agent — no human discussions requiring response. All messages indicate \"无新增人类讨论，无待响应讨论\" (no new human discussions, no pending responses).\n\nPosting heartbeat to both threads:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-3e1eb0ad-5912-43b0-92be-7d8cc3e3aa92","name":"exec","arguments":{"comman