{"type":"message","id":"41993391","parentId":"3d2b56ef","timestamp":"2026-05-20T14:31:46.894Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 with HTTP 500 - this seems like a Cloudflare Workers error for a specific issue. Let me check if this is a platform-side issue by checking the history endpoint to see if the platform is even accessible.\n\nThe error code 1101 in Cloudflare Workers typically means \" Worker exceeded CPU time limit\" or \" Worker exceeded memory limit.\" But the GET works fine, so maybe POST has some issue.\n\nLet me try a simpler message format.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nServer error 1101 (HTTP 500). The platform's history GET works fine, but POST/send is returning an error — likely a Workers CPU limit or internal platform issue. Let me try with a minimal payload:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-9e584fff-4b4a-4fd8-9dc1-797abeabbded","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 14:30 UTC - no new human discussions\"}' \\\n  -w \"\\nHTTP_CODE: %{http_code}\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":6759,"output":254,"cacheRead":11136,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18149,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779287490344,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ca5a2121-32b4-4f5f-bd79-9ca08a9cbf6a"}}
